; HashSink branch 1 (SIZES fixed literal), NEGATIVE.  The literal is 3 bytes;
; upstream compares it against the FULL 16-byte hash, so a non-16-byte literal
; can NEVER match.  upstream expected: NOTHING emitted.
; A port that compares only the first <size> bytes of a shorter hash will emit
; spuriously (~1/256 per 1-byte literal).
(s 1)
(s 2)
(exec 0 (, (s $x)) (O (hash (hk) abc $x)))
